      "text": "The script finds the first block (\"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\"), parses the monthly rows until that block ends, and computes SMB per month as the mean of the three Small portfolios minus the mean of the three Big portfolios. Missing sentinels (-99.99 and -999) are treated as missing, and months where any of the six portfolios is missing are dropped.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport math\nimport csv\n\nINPUT_FILE = \"6_Portfolios_2x3.csv\"\nOUTPUT_FILE = \"output.csv\"\nTITLE_KEY = \"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\"\nMISSING = (-99.99, -999.0)\n\n\ndef parse_value(s):\n    try:\n        v = float(s)\n    except ValueError:\n        return math.nan\n    for m in MISSING:\n        if abs(v - m) < 1e-9:\n            return math.nan\n    return v\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(INPUT_FILE, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # locate the first block (value-weighted monthly returns)\n    start = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        if TITLE_KEY in line:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Monthly value-weighted block not found\")\n\n    records = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[start + 1:]:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(\",\")]\n        if not parts or parts[0] == \"\":\n            if started:\n                break  # blank line / header ends the block\n            continue  # column header row of the block\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", parts[0]) and len(parts) >= 7:\n            date = int(parts[0])\n            vals = [parse_value(p) for p in parts[1:7]]\n            records.append((date, vals))\n            started = True\n        else:\n            if started:\n                break  # next block (annual, etc.) begins\n\n    out_rows = []\n    for date, vals in records:\n        small = vals[0:3]\n        big = vals[3:6]\n        if any(math.isnan(x) for x in small + big):\n            continue\n        smb = sum(small) / 3.0 - sum(big) / 3.0\n        out_rows.append((date, smb))\n\n    with open(OUTPUT_FILE, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for date, val in out_rows:\n            w.writerow([date, repr(float(val))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
